								<div id="contentForThisGame_ctn">
				</div>
									<div data-panel="{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;PanelGroup&quot;}" id="aboutThisGame" class="game_page_autocollapse" style="max-height: 850px;">
						<div id="game_area_description" class="game_area_description">
							<h2>About This Game</h2>
							<h2 class="bb_tag" >THE PHONE RANG AFTER TWELVE YEARS IN A BOX</h2><p class="bb_paragraph" >Haru is spending the last week of summer at grandma's house in <strong>Wasure-machi</strong> — «the Forgotten Town». In the storeroom, inside a cardboard box, an old yellow flip phone switches itself on. Inside it lives <strong>Denpa</strong>: a sarcastic AI stuck forever at 4% battery, and the only thing in the world that can see <strong>tsukumogami</strong> — the spirits that grow inside objects people stopped caring about.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><p class="bb_paragraph" >The umbrella grandma lost in 1987 has been waiting on the stairs the whole time. It is <i>thrilled</i> to see you.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><h2 class="bb_tag" >POINT. FOCUS. SNAP.</h2><p class="bb_paragraph" >Raise the TsukuLens and the town turns violet. Something is breathing inside that bush, under that vending machine, behind that shutter. Hold your breath, frame it, take the photo — a good shot earns you a friend, a bad shot earns you a blurry thumb and a spirit that is now <i>annoyed</i>.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><h2 class="bb_tag" >161 SPIRITS, AND NOT ONE OF THEM IS NORMAL</h2><p class="bb_paragraph" >A raincoat that never dried. A stapler that appointed itself a judge. A vending machine with strong opinions about loyalty. Every spirit has a tribe, a personality (shy, cocky, sleepyhead…), a favourite snack and a bond that grows when you feed it.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><h2 class="bb_tag" >THE WHEEL</h2><p class="bb_paragraph" >Six friends on a spinning wheel: three at the front fighting, three at the back catching their breath. Spin to rotate, aim with the camera, purify the cursed, throw snacks, and when the gauge fills — pull the trigger on a Burst and hit the rhythm.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><h2 class="bb_tag" >A TOWN THAT LIVES ON YOUR CLOCK</h2><p class="bb_paragraph" >The calendar inside the game is <strong>your</strong> calendar. Festivals arrive when they arrive. A full moon is a full moon. The boss of the week rotates every real Monday, and the ghost bus only stops on Tuesdays — at places that do not exist.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><h2 class="bb_tag" >WHAT ELSE IS IN THERE</h2><ul class="bb_ul"><li><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>14 places</strong>: the town, a hot spring, a beach festival, a neon city, a landfill kingdom, a school at midnight, an abandoned hospital, the sewers, a dead train tunnel, the spirit back-alley, and the same town in <strong>1987</strong>.</p></li><li><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>The Tsukumo League</strong>: eight rivals scattered across the world, and a tournament that will humble you.</p></li><li><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>The Tower of the Forgotten</strong>: 50 floors, random modifiers, no mercy.</p></li><li><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>Fishing, gachapon, karaoke duels, menko, cooking, a bug net, an onsen, a TV channel, rumours, photo quests and a free photo mode</strong> with filters, stickers and frames.</p></li><li><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>Your own room</strong> to decorate with everything you drag home, and your photos framed on the wall.</p></li><li><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>Two-player co-op</strong> where the second player is Denpa: a cursor that marks targets and throws snacks.</p></li></ul><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><h2 class="bb_tag" >THE TONE</h2><p class="bb_paragraph" >Warm, silly and occasionally sad, in the way that only a story about things people threw away can be. Denpa will insult you. You will grow fond of a stapler. Around chapter six you may need a moment.</p><p class="bb_paragraph" ></p><p class="bb_paragraph" ><strong>Isekai Games</strong></p>						</div>
					</div>
